+# Wire serialization format
+
+Records are serialized as Markdown files with YAML frontmatter (`.muninn/records/<kind>/<id>.md`), where the frontmatter contains metadata fields (id, kind, subject, relation, object, origin, trust, created_at, etc.) and the body is literal narrative text. This format enables records to be versioned, diffed, and imported without Muninn, while SQLite (`.muninn/muninn.db`) serves as the operational truth for querying. Records may also be exported to or imported from JSONL format for interoperability, with imported records receiving `origin: imported` and trust level 0 unless provenance is explicitly carried in the source file.
